      "message": "CPP \u0027new\u0027 will still abort on OOM, so it will never be nullptr.\n\nAlso - no need to copy the \u0027delete\u0027 everywhere.\n\nOne way to do it:\n\n```\nstd::unique_ptr\u003cuint8_t*, decltype(free)\u003e buffer(static_cast\u003cuint8_t*\u003e(malloc(kChunkSize)), \u0026free);\n```\n\nThen - it will automatically be deleted, and buffer.get() will be nullptr (instead of throwing an exception). It\u0027s fine to mix the C call and C++ calls, they all go to the same heap, but the CPP STL will throw exceptions 😞",
